{"case":901,"commit":"cccc2e3bfd98f2d41410294ab52f79dc18fa1002","event":"ruling","failed_agent":null,"failure_reason":null,"findings":0,"hash":"dd9f760d1bacc468dac9869e83866f4ba4f1dacf2ad8fa1b6c8fe1baa1504e20","invocation":"20260929T154957.277907+0000-82359","prev":"745bdb86f54a2b33ed5359a87c3a32e1b7455f0255d655d490c32588068c0d16","prompts":"5b8510cd900aa9da58e06fd2a865f94df5ede1bdb3c73006077576411858ea61","ruling":{"amount_sgd":null,"confidence":0.6,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"explanation":"RIDER — your $5.00 no-show charge is not being refunded today, and it is not being upheld either: the case goes to a human reviewer with the money held. DRIVER — no compensation is payable on this record. Both of you are reading the same broken instrument, and it settles nothing.\n\nThe charge can only stand if the driver carries all four limbs of POL-NS-01. He carries limb (a) — trip record TRIP-2026-09945 has an 08:43:00 arrival marker — and the reason-code half of limb (d) (cancelled by the driver at 08:51:00 on RIDER_NO_SHOW). Limbs (b) and (c) both run on the GPS trace EV-GPS-00901, and that trace cannot be read. Not one of its fixes carries a reported horizontal accuracy, so under POL-NS-02 every fix is evidence of neither presence nor absence and none establishes arrival; the derived qualifying_fix_count is 0. The trace is impaired for policy under POL-NS-08(b): gaps of 180 s, 240 s and 180 s inside the waiting window exceed the 120 s limb, the window 08:43–08:51 holds four fixes against the six required, and no rider track was supplied. Its weight is 0.6 (LOW_SAMPLE_RATE, PARTIAL_RECORD).\n\nThat impairment decides the case. The arrival and dwell facts are carried by the GPS trace alone. The trip record's 08:43:00 marker was auto-confirmed from the same GPS measurement, so it is one carrier, not two. The chat log EV-CHAT-00901 (weight 1.0) does not carry the fact: POL-NS-01(c) measures dwell from qualifying in-geofence GPS fixes, and the driver's own messages record only that he sent them — the clause reads the trace, not the log, and POL-NS-03 reads the chat log only to allocate fault. Where the test admitted no reading at all, an account offered in its place stands in for the test and neither lifts the cap nor stops the impaired trace being the only evidence. Limbs (b) and (c) are therefore undecided, not failed: an undecided limb supports neither the charge nor a refund on those grounds.\n\nSo POL-NS-08's closing sentence and POL-NS-09(e) apply: the sole evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under the clause's own limbs, the case escalates, and the $5.00 is held rather than collected or refunded. The same result follows from POL-NS-09(a), because the confidence this record supports is capped at the trace's 0.6, below the 0.70 floor.\n\nOn the specific arguments. RIDER, your claims that POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 give you a full refund are rejected as affirmative grounds — the zero dwell and zero qualifying fixes measure the trace's missing accuracy data, not the driver's conduct, and POL-NS-02's own drafting note calls a trace too sparse to raise three in-radius readings impaired rather than proof of absence. DRIVER, your POL-NS-04 arguments are accepted (the rider sent no locating message during the window, and you both replied in chat and placed the 08:47:05 in-app call), so that clause does not exonerate the rider; your POL-NS-05 point is accepted (the trace's minimum distance to the pin is 0 m, so the marker is not false and no false-arrival referral arises); your chat-log dwell claim is rejected for the reason above; and POL-NS-07 compensation is not reached, because it presupposes a chargeable fee and the fee is not established — and escalation displaces it in any event. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is null on this record, and prior_no_show_flags was rightly not substituted for it.\n\nBoth sides disclosed the ledger defect, and it is real: the fare breakdown charged $5.00 while fee_schedule yields $4.00 as the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee ($4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee ($4.00) — a $1.00 difference, a POL-NS-08(d) defect. Because escalation is terminal and holds the whole fee, I do not dispose of it here. Whether the $5.00 should be reconciled to $4.00, and whether the driver in fact arrived at Tiong Bahru Plaza and held the 300-second STANDARD minimum between 08:43 and 08:51, are the questions the reviewer must settle. The escalation packet — both briefs, the admissibility pre-pass report, every clause relied on and this reasoning — goes to human review. No referral is added: no clause on these facts produces one.\n\nThe judge was asked 4 times on the same inputs and every draft agreed on this ruling, so it is carried unanimously (vote agreement 1.00).","referrals":[],"ruling":"ESCALATE"},"seq":32,"ts":"2026-09-29T15:57:11.468650+00:00"}
